  {
    "id": "crc_tumour_budding",
    "name": "CRC Tumour Budding (ITBCC)",
    "description": "CRC Clinical suite — reuses the CRC Tissue Segmentation backbone to read the ICCR 'Tumour budding' element.\nBuds are detached tumour objects of 1–4 cells (cell count estimated from area) at the invasive front; the grade is the maximum bud count in a 0.785 mm² (20×) hotspot: Bd1 (0–4), Bd2 (5–9), Bd3 (≥10).\nRun on the deepest, transmural tumour block. HE-based screening — pan-cytokeratin is the ITBCC adjunct in equivocal cases. Set 'Reuse existing segmentation' to chain after the pT tool with no re-inference.",
    "category": "CRC Clinical",
    "supports_batch": false,
    "stain_compatibility": ["HE"],
    "estimated_minutes": 8,
    "result_type": "tumour_budding",
